# researcher Architecture

`researcher` is a research-team workspace and manuscript composer, built as a
fork of Twenty (an open-source CRM). It keeps Twenty's object, view and
navigation machinery and grafts a research domain onto it — grants, grant
discovery, applications, obligations, projects, datasets, references and
manuscripts — plus a composer that imports an existing paper, formats it
against a target journal, and exports DOCX/PDF/HTML/JATS.

## The runtime: browser-first, no backend

**The research app runs without the Twenty backend.** A browser-side data
bridge serves the standard object machinery from IndexedDB (Dexie), so the
whole app builds to a static site with no server, no account and no database.

```bash
npx nx build twenty-shared   # once
npx nx start twenty-front    # http://localhost:3001/demo
```

Port is **3001** (`packages/twenty-front/vite.config.ts`), and the nx target is
`start` — there is no `dev` target. On localhost the local bridge engages
automatically. A bare `/` is an empty workspace by design; `/demo` seeds the
sample dataset and `/reset` wipes IndexedDB.

Runtime modes are resolved in `local-db/twenty-local/isLocalTwentyDataMode.ts`:

| Mode      | Storage                          | Used by                                  |
| --------- | -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `local`   | Dexie / IndexedDB in the browser | the static build; the default on localhost |
| `convex`  | a Convex deployment (`convex/`)  | optional backend parity; not the default  |
| in-memory | RAM                              | tests                                     |

## Tech Stack

- **Frontend (the app)**: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Jotai for state, Linaria
  for zero-runtime CSS-in-JS, Lingui for i18n (`src/locales/*.po`)
- **Data layer (the app)**: Dexie/IndexedDB bridge under
  `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/local-db/`, which answers the same GraphQL
  the CRM core expects — Apollo Client still sits in front of it
- **Vendored upstream server (not run by default)**: NestJS, TypeORM,
  PostgreSQL, Redis, GraphQL Yoga, BullMQ. `twenty-server`, Postgres, Redis and
  the worker matter **only** for work on the upstream CRM server. Do not assume
  they are running, and do not add app features that require them.
- **Monorepo**: Nx workspace managed with Yarn 4

## Package Structure

```
packages/
├── twenty-front/          # React app — this is where the research fork lives
├── twenty-shared/         # Common types and utilities (build this first)
├── twenty-ui/             # Shared UI component library
├── twenty-server/         # Vendored upstream NestJS API — not run by this fork
├── twenty-emails/         # Email templates
├── twenty-utils/          # Dev-environment scripts
├── twenty-e2e-testing/    # Playwright E2E tests
└── …                      # Further vendored upstream packages (docs, website,
                           #   cli, sdk, zapier, apps, …)
convex/                    # Optional Convex parity runtime
```

The research domain is **not** a package — it lives inside the frontend:

```
packages/twenty-front/src/modules/local-db/
├── data-source/          # The GraphQL-over-Dexie data source and Apollo providers
├── twenty-local/         # Bridge modes, seeding, workspace reset
└── research/             # Research objects, views, nav, seed data
    ├── manuscript/       # Composer: import, tokens, citations, exports
    ├── import-wizard/    # Upload → map → review → commit → rollback
    └── components/       # Composer and editor UI
```

Before working under `local-db/research/`, read
`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/local-db/research/AGENTS.md`,
`docs/manuscript-format.md` and
`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/local-db/research/README.md`.

## Key Principles
- **Functional components only** (no classes)
- **Named exports only** (no default exports)
- **Types over interfaces** (except for extending third-party)
- **String literals over enums** (except GraphQL)
- **No 'any' type allowed**
- **Event handlers over useEffect** for state updates
